# {{PROJECT_NAME_MARKDOWN}}

Generated by ZeroBotForge as a standalone TypeScript Telegram bot project.

## Requirements

- Node.js {{NODE_VERSION}} or later
- A Telegram bot token created with BotFather
- {{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} package manager

## Configure

1. Install dependencies with `{{INSTALL_COMMAND}}`.
2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.
3. Set `{{TOKEN_ENV_VAR}}` in `.env` to your bot token. Keep `.env` private and do not commit it.
4. Review `project.json` and the generated TypeScript files before running the bot.

## Run locally

- Development: `{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run dev`
- TypeScript build: `{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run build`
- Run compiled output: `{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} run start`

Run these commands from this project directory. The generated program reads `project.json` from the current working directory.

## Generated runtime behavior

- The `/start` command runs the active flow, or the first flow if no active flow is set.
- Text, image, button, and choice nodes are processed from the exported flow data.
- Button and choice callback data is generated per selection and checked against the originating chat and user.
- Action nodes never execute code supplied by project data. Until a trusted operation registry is implemented in this standalone project, an action reports that it is unregistered and follows its failure connection when present.
- The exported project has no real bot token. Credentials are read only from the environment variable named above.

The generated runtime is independent of the ZeroBotForge source tree. It depends only on its declared npm dependencies and the files in this directory.
